<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kavad I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">473–531</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kavad I was Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/negus-nagast">King of Kings</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from 488 to 496 and again from 498 or 499 to 531. He owed his throne to Hephthalite support and, after nobles deposed him for favouring the Mazdakite movement, regained it with a Hephthalite army. His later reign saw wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> and the suppression of the Mazdakites, and he was succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-i">Khosrow I</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kavad-i.jpg" alt="Kavad I" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: None · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plate_with_king_hunting_rams_(white_background).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
